{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-21768-r4523476","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Fried Rice","sourcePageId":21768,"sourceRevision":"4523476","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-07-13T19:13:00Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Fried%20Rice&oldid=4523476","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:54:20.218Z","sourceCategories":["Category:East Asian recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using bean sprout","Category:Recipes using beef","Category:Recipes using bok choy","Category:Recipes using carrot","Category:Recipes using chicken","Category:Recipes using rice","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Vegan recipes","Category:Vegetarian recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"1ac0537e93ebbd0a8ba697f0207541471d93423927437a19e66bc5ab6fa47eff","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary|category=Rice recipes|servings=4 persons|time=20 minutes|difficulty=2|Image=[[Image:Fried rice by Adonis Chen in Keelung, Taiwan.jpg|300px]]}}\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Rice Recipes|Rice Recipes]]\n\n'''Fried rice''' is a simple dish that is easily modified and can be prepared in as little as five minutes. You may choose which ingredients to use and how much to use. Ingredients can be substituted and leftovers work great! \n==Ingredients==\n* Cooked [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]] (leftover rice that has been left refrigerated works well)\n* [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|Soy sauce]]\n* [[Cookbook:Oil|Oil]]\n* [[Cookbook:Peas|Peas]]\n* [[Cookbook:Bean Sprout|Bean sprouts]]\n* [[Cookbook:Bok Choy|Bok choy]]\n* [[Cookbook:Kidney Bean|Kidney beans]]\n* [[Cookbook:Mushroom|Mushroom]]\n* [[Cookbook:Carrot|Carrot]]\n* [[Cookbook:Sweetcorn|Sweet corn]]\n* Fried [[Cookbook:Tofu|tofu]]\n* [[Cookbook:Egg|Egg]]\n* Aromatics (e.g. [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], [[Cookbook:shallot|shallot]], [[Cookbook:scallion|scallion]], [[Cookbook:garlic|garlic]])\n\n===Spices===\n* [[Cookbook:Black Pepper|Black pepper]]\n* [[Cookbook:Sugar|Sugar]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n*[[Cookbook:chilli pepper|Chilli pepper]]\n*Fried rice spice\n===Meat (optional)===\nOptionally, cooked meat can be included. Leftovers work here too. \n* [[Cookbook:Chicken|Chicken]]\n* Char siu (Chinese barbecue [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]])\n* Marinated [[Cookbook:Beef|beef]]\n* [[Cookbook:Pork|Pork]]\n* [[Cookbook:Seafood|Seafood]] (add [[Cookbook:Curry Powder|curry powder]] for curry flavor)\n* [[Cookbook:Prawn|Prawns]]\n*[[Cookbook:shrimp|Shrimps]]\n\n==Procedure==\n===Prepare ingredients===\n#If using tofu, cook it.\n#If using onions, dice them into whatever size you prefer. \n#If using bok choy, separate the stalk part from the leaf part. Slice the leaf part crosswise into ¾-inch-thick strips, then tear the strips into 2-inch pieces. These pieces will be treated much like the bean sprouts, though perhaps with slightly more cooking. The stalk part will be treated as celery.\n#If using bean sprouts, wash them and discard any that are not white and crunchy.\n#If using meat, slice into desired sized pieces and cook.\n\n===Cooking===\n#Add a generous amount of oil to a large [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|frying pan]] (more than you think you'd need) to avoid sticking. If using a type of sausage or other excessively fatty meat, not as much oil may be needed because of the amount of fat. \n#Add the rice. Cook over the stove on medium-high heat.\n#Add the soy sauce, meat(s), eggs, and all vegetables except the onions and bean sprouts.\n#Add pepper, a pinch or two of sugar, and optionally some added salt. \n#Add the tofu, bean sprouts, and onion when the rice is almost done (depending on how fried you want them), being careful not to overcook them.\n\n[[Category:Vegan recipes]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:East Asian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bean sprout]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bok choy]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Fried Rice","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"Cooked rice (leftover rice that has been left refrigerated works well)","sourceText":"Cooked rice (leftover rice that has been left refrigerated works well)","amountText":"Cooked rice (leftover rice that has been left refrigerated works well)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"Soy sauce","sourceText":"Soy sauce","amountText":"Soy sauce","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"Oil","sourceText":"Oil","amountText":"Oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"Peas","sourceText":"Peas","amountText":"Peas","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"Bean sprouts","sourceText":"Bean sprouts","amountText":"Bean sprouts","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"Bok choy","sourceText":"Bok choy","amountText":"Bok choy","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"Kidney beans","sourceText":"Kidney beans","amountText":"Kidney beans","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8",